{
  "total": 62.968,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Why is the richest bear in the valley",
      "start": 0.25,
      "end": 2.426
    },
    {
      "text": "eating dinner alone?",
      "start": 2.546,
      "end": 4.082
    },
    {
      "text": "Barnaby had more gold than anyone.",
      "start": 4.382,
      "end": 6.771
    },
    {
      "text": "Three vaults. Forty servants.",
      "start": 6.891,
      "end": 8.747
    },
    {
      "text": "And every Sunday, he counted it.",
      "start": 9.047,
      "end": 11.138
    },
    {
      "text": "Coin by coin.",
      "start": 11.258,
      "end": 12.581
    },
    {
      "text": "His neighbor, Pip, had almost nothing.",
      "start": 12.881,
      "end": 15.398
    },
    {
      "text": "A small house. One bowler hat.",
      "start": 15.518,
      "end": 17.993
    },
    {
      "text": "But every Sunday, Pip's table was full.",
      "start": 18.293,
      "end": 20.896
    },
    {
      "text": "Friends. Laughter.",
      "start": 21.196,
      "end": 22.561
    },
    {
      "text": "Bread for everyone.",
      "start": 22.681,
      "end": 24.11
    },
    {
      "text": "One winter, Barnaby got sick.",
      "start": 24.41,
      "end": 26.629
    },
    {
      "text": "He rang the bell.",
      "start": 26.929,
      "end": 28.316
    },
    {
      "text": "Nobody came.",
      "start": 28.436,
      "end": 29.631
    },
    {
      "text": "His servants were paid to clean.",
      "start": 29.931,
      "end": 31.787
    },
    {
      "text": "Not to care.",
      "start": 31.907,
      "end": 33.102
    },
    {
      "text": "So he walked to Pip's house,",
      "start": 33.402,
      "end": 35.109
    },
    {
      "text": "through the snow.",
      "start": 35.229,
      "end": 36.488
    },
    {
      "text": "And Pip opened the door,",
      "start": 36.788,
      "end": 38.559
    },
    {
      "text": "like he'd been waiting for years.",
      "start": 38.679,
      "end": 40.684
    },
    {
      "text": "Why did you never come before?",
      "start": 40.984,
      "end": 43.053
    },
    {
      "text": "Barnaby had no answer.",
      "start": 43.353,
      "end": 44.974
    },
    {
      "text": "Grey, the wolf, watched from the street.",
      "start": 45.274,
      "end": 47.727
    },
    {
      "text": "And smiled.",
      "start": 47.847,
      "end": 49.127
    },
    {
      "text": "Because he knew something Barnaby didn't.",
      "start": 49.427,
      "end": 51.752
    },
    {
      "text": "You can count your gold every Sunday.",
      "start": 52.052,
      "end": 54.484
    },
    {
      "text": "But at your funeral,",
      "start": 54.784,
      "end": 56.299
    },
    {
      "text": "nobody counts the gold.",
      "start": 56.419,
      "end": 58.104
    },
    {
      "text": "They count who showed up.",
      "start": 58.404,
      "end": 60.068
    }
  ]
}